<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Wars of Religion</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as religious civil war</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Wars of Religion were a series of civil wars between Catholics and Protestants (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a>) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the second half of the sixteenth century. They ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-nantes">Edict of Nantes</a> in 1598. The decades of conflict delayed serious French colonisation overseas, holding back the early growth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion.jpg" alt="French Wars of Religion" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Dubois 1529-1584 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_masacre_de_San_Bartolom%C3%A9,_por_Fran%C3%A7ois_Dubois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
